<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Ch06_P04_Ex6_find_M</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>(a) The product \({@t0@} \times {@t0+1@} \times {@t0+2@} \times {@t0+3@} = {@P0@}\) is 1 less than a perfect square. Find a whole number \(M\) with \({@P0@} = M^2 - 1\).</p>
<div>\(M =\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]]</div>
<div>[[feedback:prt1]]</div>
<p>(b) Now the general case. Let the four consecutive integers be \({@n+shft@}\), \({@n+shft+1@}\), \({@n+shft+2@}\) and \({@n+shft+3@}\), where \(n\) is an integer. Find \(M\), a polynomial in \(n\), such that their product equals \(M^2 - 1\).</p>
<div>\(M =\) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]]</div>
<div>[[feedback:prt2]]</div>]]></text></questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>The idea is to pair the outer two numbers and the inner two. The two products differ by 2, and a product of two numbers that differ by 2 is 1 less than a perfect square: \(t(t + 2) = t^2 + 2t = (t + 1)^2 - 1\).</p>
<p>(a) \({@t0@} \times {@t0+3@} = {@onum@}\) and \({@t0+1@} \times {@t0+2@} = {@onum+2@}\), so the product is \({@onum@} \times {@onum+2@} = {@onum+1@}^2 - 1\). So \(M = {@Mnum@}\) (or \(-{@Mnum@}\)).</p>
<p>(b) The same pairing: the outer product is \({@douter@}\) and the inner product is \({@dinner@}\), which is 2 more. Writing \(t = {@douter@}\), the product is \(t(t + 2) = (t + 1)^2 - 1\), so \(M = {@taM@}\). This is an integer for every integer \(n\), so the product of any four consecutive integers is 1 less than a perfect square.</p>]]></text></generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>2</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1000000</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026062900</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables><text><![CDATA[/* [shift of the representation, first integer of the numerical example] */
vpick: rand([[0, 3], [-1, 4], [-2, 5], [-3, 6], [1, 7]]);
shft: vpick[1];
t0: vpick[2];
P0: t0*(t0+1)*(t0+2)*(t0+3);
Mnum: t0^2 + 3*t0 + 1;
/* Outer-pair product; the inner pair is onum + 2. */
onum: t0*(t0+3);
/* Inner-pair product, and a wrong value for the tests (intnum needs a single integer). */
inum: onum + 2;
Mwrong: Mnum + 3;
PP: expand((n+shft)*(n+shft+1)*(n+shft+2)*(n+shft+3));
taM: expand((n+shft)^2 + 3*(n+shft) + 1);
/* Diagnostics: a pair product taken as M. */
douter: expand((n+shft)*(n+shft+3));
dinner: expand((n+shft+1)*(n+shft+2));
s_assert(is(Mnum^2 - 1 = P0), true);
s_assert(is(expand(taM^2 - 1 - PP) = 0), true);
s_assert(is(expand(douter - taM + 1) = 0 and expand(dinner - taM - 1) = 0), true);
validate_poly(ex) := block([e], e: ev(expand(ex), simp),
  if not(every(lambda([v], member(v, [n])), listofvars(ex))) then "Use only the letter \\(n\\)."
  else if not(polynomialp(e, [n])) then "Enter a polynomial in \\(n\\), such as n^2 - 4*n + 2."
  else "");
]]></text></questionvariables>
